

Sahachara Ayurveda Operations System
## UI, Navigation, Pages, and Workflow Reference

**Purpose:** Source-grounded implementation reference for rebuilding the current system's user interface and operational behavior.

**Scope:** This report describes the implemented Next.js frontend, shared `@sahachara/ui` shell, NestJS API contracts, and Prisma domain model. It is not a screenshot specification: the repository does not include a live authenticated session or populated production dataset. Components render data-dependent details at runtime, so the source links below remain the authoritative implementation reference for exact field labels, validation text, and conditional states.

---

## 1. Product and technical shape

Sahachara is an Ayurveda clinic operations application. The repository implements:

- A Next.js App Router frontend using React 19 and IBM Carbon Design System v11.
- A reusable UI package (`@sahachara/ui`) containing the enterprise shell, data display, feedback, and layout primitives.
- A NestJS REST API mounted at `/api/v1`.
- A PostgreSQL/Prisma domain model, with shared TypeScript contracts in `@sahachara/types`.

The browser UI is composed from Carbon components and app-specific pages. It is not a static mockup: lists, records, status actions, and many metrics are driven by API data. A faithful rebuild therefore needs both the visual shell and the workflow/state behavior described below.

### Global visual foundation

- Document language is English. Root layout supplies IBM Plex Sans and IBM Plex Mono, Carbon `g10` as the initial theme, and app metadata. See [`layout.tsx`](../apps/web/src/app/layout.tsx).
- The shell uses the app title **Ayurveda Operations** and prefix **SAHACHARA**. Login and activation are rendered outside the authenticated enterprise shell. See [`app-shell.tsx`](../apps/web/src/components/app-shell.tsx).
- App-wide fonts are IBM Plex Sans (weights 300–700) and IBM Plex Mono (400–600), both Latin subsets with `display: swap`. Most colors come from Carbon theme variables; app accents include `#0f62fe`, with green/yellow/red status dots `#24a148`, `#f1c21b`, and `#da1e28`. See [`globals.scss`](../apps/web/src/app/globals.scss).
- Common page composition uses a centered, columnar `PageContainer` (maximum width 1600px, 1.5rem vertical gaps), `PageHeader` (optional breadcrumbs, title, description, status and actions), sections, Carbon cards/tables, and status tags. See [`page-container.tsx`](../packages/ui/src/components/layout/page-container.tsx), [`page-header.tsx`](../packages/ui/src/components/layout/page-header.tsx), [`metric-card.tsx`](../packages/ui/src/components/data-display/metric-card.tsx), and [`operational-data-table.tsx`](../packages/ui/src/components/data-display/operational-data-table.tsx).
- Metric tiles use uppercase 12px labels, 28px values, optional status dots/trends/icons, and a minimum height of 120px. Standard operational tables use compact Carbon tables, a toolbar search, zebra rows, pagination, loading skeletons, and defined error/empty states.
- Shell geometry in global CSS: 48px header; 256px expanded sidebar; 64px collapsed sidebar; 44px navigation links. Main content offsets around the header/sidebar and uses 2rem desktop side padding. At widths ≤1056px the sidebar becomes a hidden/off-canvas 256px drawer and the main content loses its sidebar offset; at ≤672px page gutters/padding shrink and modals use 95vw width. Data-table containers support horizontal/touch scrolling. See [`globals.scss`](../apps/web/src/app/globals.scss).
- The header switches between Carbon `g10` and `g100`. Although an architecture note mentions system sync, the implementation evidences an initial `g10` theme and a direct light/dark toggle; do not assume operating-system theme sync. See [`theme-provider.tsx`](../packages/ui/src/theme/theme-provider.tsx) and [`enterprise-header.tsx`](../packages/ui/src/components/shell/enterprise-header.tsx).
- Shell/content transitions include reduced-motion handling; shared overview/tile classes add layer-backed surfaces and subtle hover transitions. The Carbon design tokens remain the source for most text/layer/border/interactive colors.

## 2. Global shell and navigation

### Header

The top Carbon header includes, from left to right:

1. Skip-to-content control.
2. Mobile navigation drawer toggle.
3. **SAHACHARA / Ayurveda Operations** brand link to `/dashboard`.
4. Global operational search (also `⌘K` on macOS or `Ctrl+K`).
