### Settings and administration

`/settings` is a shared tabbed workspace, with nested routes selecting the initial tab:

| Route | Tab |
|---|---|
| `/settings` | Overview |
| `/settings/organization` | Organization Profile |
| `/settings/staff` | Staff Management |
| `/settings/staff/new` | New staff workflow |
| `/settings/staff/[id]` | Staff detail/workflow |
| `/settings/audit-logs` | Audit Logs |
| `/settings/configuration` | Configuration |
| `/settings/profile` | My Profile |
| `/settings/security` | Security & Sessions |

Tabs are loaded on selection and have tab-specific loading skeletons and retryable errors. Overview shows staff/session metrics. Organization profile, configuration and personal profile are editable forms with save/error/success states. Configuration covers sequence prefixes; timezone is supplied from `CLINIC_TIMEZONE` (default `Asia/Kolkata`) and currency is currently hard-coded as INR in the API response rather than organization-persisted fields. Security shows role/session summary and active device/browser sessions.

Staff Management provides role/status filters and registry, add staff, regenerate PIN, deactivate/reactivate and change-role controls. Add and activation use separate dialogs. Audit Logs filters actions, lists audit entries and opens a selected-entry detail modal.

For non-admin users, the frontend hides Organization Profile, Staff Management, Audit Logs and Configuration; Overview, My Profile and Security remain visible. Staff role choices include `SUPER_ADMIN` only when the current user is `SUPER_ADMIN`. Sources: [`settings-workspace.tsx`](../apps/web/src/components/settings/settings-workspace.tsx), tab implementations in [`apps/web/src/components/settings/`](../apps/web/src/components/settings/).

